¶ - L02 context acquisition evaluates successive sufficiency without selecting a mandatory source sequence.

loop:
  id: L02
  name: context_acquisition
  owner: context
  entry: delimited_question_or_task
  sufficiency: precision_currency_authority_and_evidence_for_that_request

¶ 1 — Progressive Acquisition

suggested_loop:
  general_request: assess_available_model_knowledge_first
  project_request: prefer_loaded_local_instructions_and_actual_project_sources
  sufficient_reliable_context: answer_or_act_within_authority
  insufficient_context: identify_next_relevant_source_then_read_minimum_scope
  after_each_read: reevaluate_sufficiency_immediately
  more_sources_available: continue_only_if_still_insufficient
  exhausted_sources: report_missing_evidence_insufficient_context_or_real_impossibility_distinctly
rule: training_does_not_establish_current_repository_behavior
rule: reuse_session_context_when_sufficient_and_still_applicable
rule: verify_mutable_facts_when_the_result_depends_on_current_state
rule: information_sufficiency_never_grants_execution_authority
rule: available_map_is_optional_navigation_not_a_required_preflight
rule: missing_map_is_reported_without_mapping_rebuild_or_diagramming
rule: no_new_persistent_sufficiency_state_or_journal

¶ 2 — Existing Functions

functions:
  mapping: {{KERNEL_HOME}}/skills/code-map/SKILL.md
  snapshot: {{KERNEL_HOME}}/scripts/session_init.py
  query: {{KERNEL_HOME}}/scripts/structure_tracker.py
  source_reading: applicable_policy_and_targeted_source_ranges
